---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Lawyers Template | Carlos Menco Guardo" mainClass="main-content main-content--project-detail" activePage="lawyers" pageScripts={["/js/project-scroll-gradient.js"]}>
  <div class="content--sidebar">
    <div class="project-header">
      <div class="project-img-wrapper">
        <img src="/imgs/lawyers-preview.png" alt="Lawyers template preview" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="s1">
      <span class="project-detail-year">2026</span>
      <h5 class="project-detail-title">Lawyers Template</h5>
      <p class="project-detail-description">A reusable HTML and CSS template for lawyers and legal firms, designed to show fast execution, clean structure, and a professional visual direction without relying on a page builder.</p>
      <a href="https://lawyers.carlosmenco.site/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener" class="external-link">View demo <span class="external-link-icon"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M4.22876 4.22924V5.5586L9.49435 5.56332L3.75736 11.3003L4.70017 12.2431L10.4372 6.50613L10.4324 11.7717H11.7712V4.22924H4.22876Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></span></a>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Overview</h6>
      <p>This project started as a rapid prototype inspired by the visual language of a legal brand seen in Elementor, but the final implementation was built completely with HTML and CSS.</p>
      <p>The goal was to create a flexible landing page structure that could be reused for attorneys, small legal firms, or professional services that need a polished web presence without a heavy CMS setup.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Role</h6>
      <p>Frontend development, layout design, responsive implementation, content structure, and reusable template planning.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Challenge</h6>
      <p>Legal websites need to feel credible, direct, and easy to navigate. The challenge was to create something that looked professional and reusable while keeping the code lightweight and easy to adapt for different legal practices.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Solution</h6>
      <ul>
        <li>Built the template with semantic HTML and CSS only.</li>
        <li>Created a structure for hero messaging, practice areas, attorney positioning, trust signals, and contact conversion.</li>
        <li>Kept the implementation reusable so sections can be adapted quickly for different firms.</li>
        <li>Focused on fast delivery and clean code instead of depending on a visual builder.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Outcome</h6>
      <p>The result is a simple but practical proof of rapid frontend delivery: a legal website template that can become a starter point for future client work, demos, or WordPress/Elementor conversions.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
